  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The People's Consultative Assembly (MPR) of Indonesia has officially postponed the plenary session for the selection and inauguration of a new vice president to December 9, 2026. This decision follows a formal request submitted by President Prabowo, which the assembly subsequently reviewed and approved. As part of the ongoing process, the President is obligated to nominate two potential candidates for the vacancy, with a submission deadline set for November 25, 2026. According to the MPR, each proposed candidate must comply with approximately 22 mandatory requirements to be considered eligible. The assembly is currently finalizing the procedural mechanisms required to conduct the selection process effectively. This legislative development follows the need to fill the vacancy created after the departure of the former vice president, ensuring continuity within the executive branch.",
